join Mama Zulu (Neutral) left
Mama Zulu: That one. Not the one beside it — that one is its cousin and it will only make you sleep.
Lindi: How do you tell them apart before they flower?
Mama Zulu: The stem. And the ground it chooses.
Lindi: The ground it — you mean the soil. The drainage.
Lindi: She's got fifty years of this. Fifty. And she's giving it away to me because her knees have got bad and she'd rather it went somewhere than nowhere.
Lindi: I keep wanting to tell her what the words are for the things she knows. And then I think — she doesn't need the words. I need the words. She just needs somebody to carry it.
